new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ai-pane-ownership-split.md
@@ -0,0 +1,97 @@
+# AI Pane Ownership Split and AI Control Center
+
+## Goal
+
+Make `AI`, `Assistant`, `LLM Chat`, and `LLM Sources` true owner panes instead
+of overlapping summary shells.
+
+## Control Center Rules
+
+- `AI` is the shared control-center pane.
+  - It owns shared status, MCP controls, AI workflows, automation suggestions,
+    runtime/performance controls, and shared operational actions.
+  - It must not own Assistant-only prompt editing, `LLM Chat` prompt editing,
+    summary prompt editing, source CRUD, or extraction compatibility controls.
+- `Assistant` is distinct from `AI`.
+  - It owns Assistant-specific behavior, retrieval/fallback status, and the
+    Assistant prompt only.
+- `Summaries` owns the summary prompt and summarizer test surface.
+- `Templates` owns advanced extraction compatibility in a collapsed advanced
+  section.
+
+## Ownership Rules
+
+- `Assistant` owns Assistant behavior only.
+  - It may show Assistant status, Assistant model status, retrieval health, and
+    Assistant fallback binding.
+  - It must not own source CRUD, raw endpoint fields, MCP controls, AI
+    workflows, automation suggestions, or shared performance controls.
+- `LLM Chat` owns raw chat binding and chat-specific status.
+  - It may show the effective chat source and allow chat binding changes.
+  - It must not own source CRUD.
+- `LLM Sources` owns saved endpoint inventory.
+  - It owns source add/edit/delete/test and role assignment to
+    `Assistant fallback`, `LLM Chat`, and `Background`.
+
+## Binding Rules
+
+- `mail.ai.source_id` remains the default saved source.
+- `mail.ai.assistant_fallback.source_id` overrides Assistant fallback only.
+- `mail.ai.llm_chat.source_id` overrides raw LLM Chat only.
+- `mail.ai.background.source_id` overrides background endpoint summaries only.
+- Empty role-specific prefs inherit the default provider/source behavior.
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+
+- Opening `AI` shows shared status, MCP controls, workflows, automation
+  suggestions, and analysis performance controls.
+- Opening `Assistant` shows no shared control-center sections.
+- Opening `Assistant` shows no saved-source editor and no raw endpoint URL or
+  token fields.
+- Opening `LLM Sources` allows full source management without opening
+  `Assistant`.
+- Opening `LLM Chat` shows and changes the raw chat binding without opening
+  `Assistant`.
+- Assistant prompt editing exists only in `Assistant`.
+- `LLM Chat` prompt editing exists only in `LLM Chat`.
+- Summary prompt editing exists only in `Summaries`.
+- Advanced extraction compatibility exists only in `Templates`.
+- Assistant fallback and LLM Chat can point at different saved sources.
+- Background endpoint use can point at a different saved source.
+- Runtime status and footer-facing summaries expose distinct bindings for
+  Assistant, `LLM Chat`, and Background.
+- Assistant model status is distinct from Summarizer model status.
+
+## Pane-Local Test Log Contract
+
+- Every pane-level `Test ...` action renders its latest result directly below
+  that pane's test-button row.
+- The pane-local log must show:
+  - timestamp
+  - target tested
+  - pass/fail/skipped state
+  - short message
+- The pane-local log must update in place on repeat runs.
+- Global/runtime status may also update, but it must not replace the pane-local
+  log surface.
+
+## Tests
+
+- Browser prefs coverage:
+  - `AI` owns shared control-center sections.
+  - `Assistant` owns Assistant-only prompt and fallback controls.
+  - `LLM Sources` owns source CRUD and role assignment.
+  - `Assistant` no longer exposes source CRUD.
+  - `LLM Chat` exposes and changes its dedicated binding.
+  - `Templates` owns extraction compatibility.
+  - pane-local test logs render in the pane where the action was triggered.
+- Xpcshell coverage:
+  - role-specific endpoint bindings override the default source.
+  - Assistant, `LLM Chat`, and Background resolve to different sources when set.
+
+## Final Reporting Format
+
+- `Planned`
+- `Implemented`
+- `Tested`
+- `Remaining gaps`
